{"nodes": [{"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_chapter1", "label": "Chapter 1 \u2014 The principles (twenty-three principles)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_p1_self_referencing", "label": "P1 \u2014 a complete index is self-referencing, \u211b(\u039b) = \u039b", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_p2_self_defending", "label": "P2 \u2014 a complete index is self-defending, \u2145 \u2265 1", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "\u2145 \u2265 1 exactly when dim q > dim p: the index must derive strictly more quantities than it assigns parameters. Without surplus there is no check."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_p7_all_questions_close", "label": "P7 \u2014 all questions must close, \u2203N : \u03a9_N = \u2205", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "First stated as though the count of open items always decreases; it does not, so closure needs a well-founded measure rather than a shrinking count, and the principle forbids claiming coherence rather than asserting gaps always close."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_p9_single_definition", "label": "P9 \u2014 one all-encompassing definition, every other dimension a perspective of it", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Its only computed case (rank(log q) = 1 over fifteen Rydberg observables) is a tautology under \u00a726.1's assembly rule; E itself is the genuine second instance, read forward, backward and as an outcome."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_p13_coherence", "label": "P13 \u2014 coherence may not be claimed while a caveat stands, COHERENT \u27fa \u03a9 = \u2205", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_p17_path_through_bounds", "label": "P17 \u2014 the path is always through the bounds", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The 1/N form is ungrounded because N is nowhere defined; the corrected form is one comparison per constraint against one per cell."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_p19_completeness", "label": "P19 \u2014 COMPLETE(X) \u27fa Q(X) = \u2205", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Strictly stronger than closure: \u039b has had E = 0 since Chapter 7 and has never had Q = \u2205. Closure is about what an index holds, completeness about what it has been asked."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_p20_language_bounds", "label": "P20 \u2014 the language in which a question is posed bounds whether it can close", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The choice of language is made when the index is built, not when the question is asked; \u00a77.1's choice of monotone two-variable bounds is what made E(X) computable."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_p21_every_language", "label": "P21 \u2014 every definition true in every mathematical language and their combinations", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An instrument, not only a criterion: when a property holds in five languages and fails in the sixth, it is the sixth expression that is wrong. A mismatched operator is a mistranslation, not a counter-example."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_p22_visibility", "label": "P22 \u2014 a complete index converts deception into disagreement", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The original claim ('no lie can exist within it') is false \u2014 an index rebuilt around a fabrication still closes with E = 0. What is true is that a stated rule contradicts a false cell in the open where an inferred rule quietly absorbs it."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_three_kinds", "label": "MECHANISM / OPERATION / RELATION \u2014 the three kinds of principle", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sorting by what a principle is, rather than by whether an expression exists, is what settles what each one owes: a relation carries content and takes no expression."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_well_founded_measure", "label": "P7's well-founded measure \u2014 the multiset of `blocks` values", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The measure is not the count of open items but a bounded, ordered stake coordinate whose multiset extension is again well-founded (Dershowitz\u2013Manna)."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_surplus_bits", "label": "Surplus \u2014 7.07 bits per cell (\u00a711.1.1)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_rule_content_vs_inferred", "label": "Rule as content versus rule as inference", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Same cell, same index: where the rule is inferred \u211b revises the bound and admits 75 impossible configurations; where it is content the cell is refused by a stated rule."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_documentary_language", "label": "The documentary language \u2014 no closure mechanism exists", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Novelty is posed in the documentary language, which has no closure mechanism, so failure to settle it is structural rather than a failure of searching."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_closure_language_table", "label": "Three closure mechanisms \u2014 tree factorisation, Gr\u00f6bner basis, quantifier elimination", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_self_feeding_loop", "label": "The self-feeding loop and its asymmetry \u2014 extensive gives repair, monotone gives absorption", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A structure that closes heals what you remove and swallows what you insert, so self-consistency defends against loss and never against invention \u2014 the formal reason Chapter 16 cannot rely on self-reference alone."}], "edges": [{"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_chapter1", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_p1_self_referencing", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_chapter1", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_p2_self_defending", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_chapter1", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_p7_all_questions_close", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_chapter1", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_p9_single_definition", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_chapter1", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_p13_coherence", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_chapter1", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_p17_path_through_bounds", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_chapter1", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_p19_completeness", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter1-principles.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_chapter1", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter1_principles_p20_language_bounds", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "conf